# Pairs with CausalOrder. Replaying a dead-letter removes it from the queue without applying it, so it
# is no longer held back and a dependent below S is released before it.
MODULE: CausalOrderReplayDropsTheDeadLetter
TARGET: CausalOrder
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a replay removes the dead-letter without applying it, so it is neither held nor applied
PERTURBS: Replay
BOUNDS: NParts = 1

--- FIND
    /\ rApplied' = rApplied \cup {h} /\ ids' = ids \cup {h}
--- REPLACE
    \* MUTATION: removed, not applied.
    /\ UNCHANGED <<rApplied, ids>>
--- END
